                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0aa4b8af-4512-3077-afdb-3b53a59e6f6c",
                        "entry_id": "98f4cdfb-16b5-3a72-8938-6d62ffa5fbe5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Considérer comme bouc émissaire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "958fa544-1324-4a38-8b14-1ec81e058108",
                                "sense_id": "0aa4b8af-4512-3077-afdb-3b53a59e6f6c",
                                "text": "Le troupeau avachi bouc-émissairise le différent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "18dcbcc6-3816-4277-a1d9-4cbceffcf30c",
                                "sense_id": "0aa4b8af-4512-3077-afdb-3b53a59e6f6c",
                                "text": "Mais lorsqu’il allègue que le syndicalisme a entraîné une « fonctionnarisation » des journalistes, voire une diminution qualitative de leur travail, il bouc-émissairise."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b71ddeb4-0531-41db-b59d-a89dca39bd25",
                                "sense_id": "0aa4b8af-4512-3077-afdb-3b53a59e6f6c",
                                "text": "Évitez de vous « bouc-émissairiser » : passez rapidement sur le négatif (même réaliste et partagé)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6b7c9d3e-217f-47f0-b669-412a270c2f3e",
                        "source_entry_id": "98f4cdfb-16b5-3a72-8938-6d62ffa5fbe5",
                        "source_sense_id": "0aa4b8af-4512-3077-afdb-3b53a59e6f6c",
                        "target_lang_word": "scapegoat",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "scapegoat",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1d107fe5-b646-385e-a8bc-a534049386e6",
                                        "entry_id": "dc9742c5-0e99-3bed-8fb2-ace071539b77",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In the Mosaic Day of Atonement ritual, a goat symbolically imbued with the sins of the people, and sent out alive into the wilderness while another was sacrificed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31c9338c-ca24-4733-9aba-9947fb82367a",
                                                "sense_id": "1d107fe5-b646-385e-a8bc-a534049386e6",
                                                "text": "And Aarõ caſt lottes ouer the .ij. gootes: one lotte for the Lorde, ãd another for a ſcapegoote."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65fd9b12-4580-4306-bb0c-fdd715b70182",
                                                "sense_id": "1d107fe5-b646-385e-a8bc-a534049386e6",
                                                "text": "[…]; alluding herein unto the heart of man, and the precious bloud of our Saviour; who was typified indeed by the Goat that was ſlain, and the ſcape Goat in the wilderneſſe;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "40fb60e8-3bbc-3c0d-ac5e-3bc7639ba69c",
                                        "entry_id": "dc9742c5-0e99-3bed-8fb2-ace071539b77",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone unfairly blamed or punished for some failure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bfbf842-b869-45cb-80c1-cf859b0b1681",
                                                "sense_id": "40fb60e8-3bbc-3c0d-ac5e-3bc7639ba69c",
                                                "text": "He is making me a scapegoat for his own poor business decisions and the supply chain disruptions caused by the hurricane!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c83b14e-3694-4e0f-8ec0-f6a820c96ffa",
                                                "sense_id": "40fb60e8-3bbc-3c0d-ac5e-3bc7639ba69c",
                                                "text": "The new Secretary of State had been long sick of the perfidy and levity of the First Lord of the Treasury, and began to fear that he might be made a scapegoat to save the old intriguer who, imbecile as he seemed, never wanted dexterity where danger was to be avoided."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "scapegoat",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8cade3b8-626f-39c8-8b74-fc93954d66e2",
                                        "entry_id": "dc34ac52-9a9f-32df-b79a-9a2ab47d9db8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To unfairly blame or punish someone for some failure; to make a scapegoat of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03919210-d9ec-4913-b809-0e972c962472",
                                                "sense_id": "8cade3b8-626f-39c8-8b74-fc93954d66e2",
                                                "text": "The question we should be asking is: who benefits when migrants and refugees are scapegoated for anger about housing?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a7e4dfc-ff02-435a-a832-03b5ee1dea00",
                                                "sense_id": "8cade3b8-626f-39c8-8b74-fc93954d66e2",
                                                "text": "People tend to fear and then to scapegoat ... groups which seem to them to be fundamentally different from their own."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4726e2c4-d53c-49a5-adcc-2f99f459ef53",
                                                "sense_id": "8cade3b8-626f-39c8-8b74-fc93954d66e2",
                                                "text": "They had been used for centuries to justify or rationalize the behavior of that status and conversely to scapegoat and blame some other category of people."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfc37a08-c1b8-415c-8bd4-3a3fb745e1be",
                                                "sense_id": "8cade3b8-626f-39c8-8b74-fc93954d66e2",
                                                "text": "And I want to add, as we make these changes, we work together to improve this system, that our intention is not scapegoating and finger-pointing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "543faf3d-e39b-4942-9f7c-d0cdcc525e09",
                                                "sense_id": "8cade3b8-626f-39c8-8b74-fc93954d66e2",
                                                "text": "Then either the world or others or the self becomes the target for the human tendency to scapegoat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
